{"schema_version":"1.7.5","id":"SUSE-SU-2026:0584-1","published":"2026-02-20T10:03:22Z","modified":"2026-03-23T04:52:22.166063Z","related":["CVE-2026-2003","CVE-2026-2004","CVE-2026-2005","CVE-2026-2006","CVE-2026-2007"],"upstream":["CVE-2026-2003","CVE-2026-2004","CVE-2026-2005","CVE-2026-2006","CVE-2026-2007"],"summary":"Security update for postgresql18","details":"This update for postgresql18 fixes the following issues:\n\nUpdate to version 18.2.\n\nSecurity issues fixed:\n\n- CVE-2026-2003: improper validation of type 'oidvector' may allow disclose a few bytes of server memory (bsc#1258008).\n- CVE-2026-2004: intarray missing validation of type of input to selectivity estimator could lead to arbitrary code\n  execution (bsc#1258009).\n- CVE-2026-2005: buffer overrun in contrib/pgcrypto's PGP decryption functions could lead to arbitrary code execution\n  (bsc#1258010).\n- CVE-2026-2006: inadequate validation of multibyte character lengths could lead to arbitrary code execution\n  (bsc#1258011).\n- CVE-2026-2007: pg_trgm heap buffer overflow can cause to write pattern onto server memory (bsc#1258012).\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":"postgresql18","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Enterprise High Performance Computing 15 SP4-ESPOS","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/postgresql18&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Enterprise%20High%20Performance%20Computing%2015%20SP4-ESPOS"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"18.2-150200.5.6.1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"binaries":[{"libecpg6":"18.2-150200.5.6.1","libpq5":"18.2-150200.5.6.1","libpq5-32bit":"18.2-150200.5.6.1"}]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://ftp.suse.com/pub/projects/security/osv/SUSE-SU-2026:0584-1.json"}},{"package":{"name":"postgresql18","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Enterprise High Performance Computing 15 SP4-LTSS","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/postgresql18&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Enterprise%20High%20Performance%20Computing%2015%20SP4-LTSS"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"18.2-150